References consulted for the MikroTik decoys (nothing copied)

The MikroTik decoys in main/honeypot/tripwire.c and main/honeypot/mikrotik.c
were written from the protocol descriptions below. No code, data tables or
exploit signatures were copied from any of them; they are listed so the
sources are clear.

- MikroTik RouterOS API manual
  https://help.mikrotik.com/docs/spaces/ROS/pages/47579160/API
  Word length encoding and sentence structure (the API decoy's reader).

- tenable/routeros, 8291_honeypot (BSD-3-Clause, archived)
  https://github.com/tenable/routeros/tree/master/8291_honeypot
  Design reference: Winbox's client speaks first. That honeypot answers
  "insufficient permissions"; this decoy stays silent instead.

- Wireshark, epan/dissectors/packet-mndp.c (GPL)
  https://github.com/wireshark/wireshark/blob/master/epan/dissectors/packet-mndp.c
  Consulted for the MNDP format (4-byte header, 16-bit big-endian type and
  length records, the record numbers for MAC, identity, version, platform and
  board). Reimplemented from the format; no code copied.

- haakonnessjoen/MAC-Telnet (GPL-2.0-or-later)
  https://github.com/haakonnessjoen/MAC-Telnet
  Consulted for the MAC-Telnet header layout and packet types, the 4-byte
  MNDP solicitation, and how the client sends (IP broadcast). Reimplemented
  from the format; no code copied.
